It's a cool idea, but unfortunately the difficulty of the monsters
you see is related to Both your level and the dungeon level (the average
in fact).  As Level 1 character on Dungeon Level 30, random monster
generation won't give you anything tougher than Level 14.  That's
enough to get rid of Random Mature dragons and Purple worms.

On the other hand, the dragons and soldiers on the Castle level are
'built in' to the level,and would appear there anyway.

If anything, this Averaging thing certainly allows you have some
influence on how tough the monsters you see are.  If you ran fast
enough, your first level character might be able to get all the
way to the Gnomish Town before any hill orcs are created.  Of course,
the hobbits and gnomes would still merrily zap wands at you.
I actually play more conservatively, and as a result, for my
first ten levels or so, I out-rank all the monsters I meet.
(Shopkeepers not included)

If you really want to have fun with dungeon diving, try a
discovery mode game with a Barbarian and the following three wishes.
     blessed ring of teleport control
     three cursed scrolls of teleportation
     one favorite weapon (like Mjollnir)
With the ring and the scrolls, you can just push yourself deeper
and deeper.  Maybe one to the bottom of the first dungeon, and
then a second to go deep into Gehennom.  Depending on who you meet,
it's a great way to get fast levels!

